      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name comes from early settler John Goodrich, who arrived in the area in 1835 after traveling from Buffalo to Detroit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodrich%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Goodrich sits within Atlas Township and is part of the Flint metropolitan area, linking it to a larger regional community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodrich%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers noted the land’s rich, fertile soil, abundant timber, and plentiful water when they reached what is now Goodrich.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
